  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "orb_c",
      "defType": "meta/comment",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -364
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "Orbital sandbox\n\nBodies orbit a pair of stars that circle each other, so no orbit quite repeats: a three-body system you can play with. Every frame each body's velocity takes the pull of both stars (G·m / r², softened up close) and its position takes the new velocity — positions and velocities live in Read* / Write* state. Bodies that fall into a star or fly off are dropped.\n\n• Drag on the canvas and let go to launch a body: it flies from where you pressed, away from the cursor, faster the longer the pull.\n• Slider into `warp`: time warp (0.25× – 3×).\n• Slider into `sep`: the stars' separation (small = one star, steady Kepler orbits; wide = chaos).\n• Toggle: orbit trails (Echo).",
        "width": 560,
        "height": 300
      },
      "portValues": {
        "text": "Orbital sandbox\n\nBodies orbit a pair of stars that circle each other, so no orbit quite repeats: a three-body system you can play with. Every frame each body's velocity takes the pull of both stars (G·m / r², softened up close) and its position takes the new velocity — positions and velocities live in Read* / Write* state. Bodies that fall into a star or fly off are dropped.\n\n• Drag on the canvas and let go to launch a body: it flies from where you pressed, away from the cursor, faster the longer the pull.\n• Slider into `warp`: time warp (0.25× – 3×).\n• Slider into `sep`: the stars' separation (small = one star, steady Kepler orbits; wide = chaos).\n• Toggle: orbit trails (Echo).",
        "width": 560,
        "height": 300
      }
    },
